UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Forming Inc. operates from Richland Hills, Texas, in the Fort Worth metro area. The company was founded in 1978 by Tom Stepp, a native Texan who spent over 20 years at Bell Helicopter before renting 2,500 square feet of industrial space with a single machine and two employees—one of them his wife, Dorothy, who handled bookkeeping. Their first projects included a children''s swimming pool protector and a point-of-purchase display.

Today the firm occupies more than 45,000 square feet of manufacturing space and offers vacuum pressure forming (thermoforming), precision die-cutting, plastic fabricating, and packaging services. The thermoforming process heats plastic sheets and shapes them with vacuum or hydraulic pressure; molds are built in-house to customer specifications. Die-cutting handles materials such as paper, fabric, or thin metal for tight-tolerance components. Fabricating covers molding, machining, and forming of raw plastic into finished parts.

Stepp''s founding values—transparency, integrity, and diligence—remain central to the operation. The company emphasizes a 5S workplace organization system to maintain efficiency and consistency, and its stated mission is to exceed expectations through innovation, quality, and sustainable practices.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum pressure forming (thermoforming)", "Precision die-cutting", "Plastic fabricating", "Packaging services", "In-house mold making"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics", "Packaging", "Consumer goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house mold making to customer specifications", "5S workplace organization program for efficiency and consistency", "Over 45,000 sq ft of manufacturing capacity", "Founder-led values of transparency, integrity, and diligence", "Material selection guidance for formability, impact strength, and shrinkage"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 by Tom Stepp after 20 years at Bell Helicopter -> /", "Started with 2,500 sq ft, one machine, two employees including wife Dorothy -> /", "First products: children''s swimming pool protector and point-of-purchase display -> /", "Current manufacturing space over 45,000 sq ft -> /", "Services: vacuum pressure forming, die-cutting, fabricating, packaging services -> /", "Thermoforming process described with in-house mold creation -> /", "Die-cutting used in automotive, electronics, packaging industries -> /", "5S workplace organization program implemented -> /", "Headquarters in Richland Hills, Texas (Fort Worth area) -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Founded year 1978 -> db", "HQ city Richland Hills, state Texas -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we strive to provide quality parts, fair and competitive prices, and services that exceed customer expectations", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code