UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Mold Technology operates from Kentwood, Michigan. The company traces its roots to 1958 when Adrian Woldring founded Woldring and Associates as an electrical discharge machining (EDM) sales business. By the late 1960s the firm had shifted to building plastic injection molds, primarily for the automotive sector. After Woldring''s retirement in 1974, Gary Proos took on joint ownership and acquired the company outright in 1984.

Today the shop provides prototype and production tooling for a broad spectrum of injection molding processes. Its capabilities include standard injection molding, insert molding, second-shot overmolding, glass encapsulation, stack molds, gas assist, two-shot molding, rotary molding, and reaction injection molding (RIM).

The company''s customer base centers on the automotive industry, where it has supplied molds for decades.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Standard Injection Molding", "Insert Molding", "Second Shot Overmold", "Glass Encapsulation", "Stack Molds", "Gas Assist", "Two Shot Molding", "Rotary Molding", "Reaction Injection Molding (RIM)"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prototype and production tooling", "Wide range of injection molding processes (including two-shot, gas assist, stack molds)", "Extensive experience of management and shop floor staff", "Decades of automotive mold experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 as Woldring and Associates by Adrian Woldring -> /about-us", "Evolved to building plastic injection molds for automotive market by late 1960s -> /about-us", "Gary Proos obtained joint ownership in 1974, full ownership in 1984 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Kentwood, Michigan -> db", "Offers prototype and production tooling for wide range of molding processes -> /", "Capabilities: Standard Injection Molding, Insert Molding, Second Shot Overmold, Glass Encapsulation, Stack Molds, Gas Assist, Two Shot Molding, Rotary Molding, Reaction Injection (R.I.M.) -> /", "Serves automotive industry -> /about-us", "Emphasizes extensive experience of management and shop floor staff -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "building plastic injection molds primarily for the automotive market", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastic-mold-technology-molding-facility' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Molding Development was founded in 1985 in Sterling Heights, Michigan. The company began as a plastic injection molding resource and has since grown to serve automobile manufacturers worldwide.

The company operates a 35,000-square-foot facility equipped with a range of Van Dorn and Wittmann Battenfeld injection molding machines from 170 to 3,300 tons, supported by 10- to 40-ton cranes. Its core services include plastic injection molding, tool and mold testing, injection tryout testing, and short-run production, with capability for both steel and aluminum tooling.

Roughly 90 percent of its work serves the automotive industry, supporting OEMs, Tier 1 suppliers, and tool shops. The company also produces industrial and consumer products, as well as specialty and prototype parts for engineers and program managers.

