ith local roots -> /", "Fast turnaround for custom plastic molding development -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our primary service is to provide plastic injection molding for the automotive industry.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastic-molding-development' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Molding Manufacturing is headquartered in Berlin, Connecticut, and traces its origins to 1968 when founder George E. Danis established Danis Manufacturing Company (DAMCO Inc.) and Plastic Molding Manufacturing Inc. to serve Massachusetts'' emerging high-tech industries. The company began as a contract manufacturer for plastic injection molding and printed circuit board assembly.

Today the company operates four plants across Connecticut, Massachusetts, Indiana, and Pennsylvania, running more than 100 injection molding presses. Its capabilities span insert molding, two-shot molding, medical-grade production in an ISO 8 clean room, scientific molding, design-for-manufacturing support, precision tooling, and a range of secondary services. The operation handles everything from rapid prototyping and low-volume runs to high-cavitation, high-volume production.

The customer base spans consumer, medical, industrial, defense, transportation, connector, and railroad sectors. The company has managed thousands of projects since its founding, producing components such as housings, industrial parts, and high-volume disposable products.

Plastic Molding Manufacturing emphasizes a ''Speed, Quality, Cost'' philosophy and a long-standing commitment to re-shoring U.S. production. Differentiators cited include end-to-end in-house expertise, continuous investment in advanced molding equipment and smart-process engineering, rigorous quality management with onsite mold maintenance, and tool-transfer protocols designed to minimize downtime during supplier transitions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ISO 13485','ISO 19001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Insert molding", "Two-shot molding", "Medical/ISO 8 clean room molding", "Scientific molding", "Design for manufacturing (DFM) support", "Precision tooling", "Full-scale injection molding", "Rapid prototyping", "Low-volume production", "High-cavitation production", "Secondary services", "Onsite mold maintenance", "CMM inspection", "Statistical process control", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "PPAP & capability studies", "Root cause analysis (5 Whys, Fishbone, Fault Tree)", "8D corrective action and MRB system", "Non-conforming material/tool control", "Purchased materials traceability", "Fully documented inspection plans", "Tool transfer protocols", "Quality management via integrated ERP"], "industries": ["Consumer", "Medical", "Industrial", "Defense", "Transportation", "Connectors", "Railroad"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["100+ injection molding presses", "CMM (Coordinate Measuring Machine)", "PCDMIS Software"], "volume": "Rapid prototyping to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end in-house capabilities from design-for-manufacturing through tooling and molding", "Scalability from rapid prototyping to high-cavitation production", "Continuous investment in latest injection molding equipment and smart-process engineering", "Rigorous quality management with onsite mold maintenance and tight tolerances", "Tool transfer protocols for seamless mold transitions and re-shoring support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Berlin, CT -> db", "Founded 1968 by George E. Danis -> /about", "Four plants, 100+ presses -> / (homepage) and /about", "Capabilities: insert molding, two-shot, medical/ISO 8 clean room, scientific molding, DFM, tooling, secondary services -> / (homepage) and /about", "Industries served: consumer, medical, industrial, defense, transportation, connectors, railroad -> / (homepage)", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, ISO 13485, ISO 19001:2015 -> /quality and db", "Equipment: 100+ presses, CMM, PCDMIS -> /quality and / (homepage)", "Volume range: rapid prototyping to high-volume -> / (homepage)", "Re-shoring commitment and tool transfer protocols -> / (homepage) and /about", "Acquisition history (Res-Tech, Tech Atlantic, Northeast Mold, True Precision, Aucilla, Phillips-Moldex) -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Plastic Molding Manufacturing provided contract manufacturing for plastic injection molding and PC board assembly.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastic-molding-manufacturing-berlin-ct' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Recycling of Iowa Falls, Inc. operates from Iowa Falls, Iowa. The business traces its roots to 1986 when Hammer''s Plastic Recycling began processing mixed plastic and manufacturing products from commingled material. In 1984, Hammer''s had formed Plastic Recycling, Inc. to design and build a production facility for recycling mixed-plastic waste. The company won the Iowa Governor''s Award in 1988. New management took over in 1997, and the name changed to Plastic Recycling of Iowa Falls in 1999.

The company manufactures a range of recycled-plastic products including park benches, picnic tables, planters, trash receptacles, traffic safety items such as car stops and speed bumps, landscape timbers, posts, dimensional lumber, and custom-molded parts. Production runs on automated lines for large-profile items, supported by patented equipment that enables custom molding with low-cost mold design. The firm''s unique molds and processes are protected by multiple U.S. and international patents.

Customers include the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, the National Park system, state and city governments, and industrial manufacturers. Washington State Parks has installed over 2,000 picnic tables; Marshall Engines uses recycled-plastic skids for shipping remanufactured engines; the Smithsonian Institution relied on the lumber for supporting a historic bell; and the City of Norwalk Parks and Recreation purchased hex tables for its aquatic center.

The company was founded to address the landfill crisis by turning plastic waste into a community resource. It emphasizes a minimum 96% recycled content (by weight) with additives limited to 4%, UV stabilizers molded in, and products that require no painting, staining, or sealing and resist warping, splintering, and rot.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automated production of large-profile recycled plastic products", "Custom molding with patented equipment", "Mold design and fabrication", "Mixed plastic processing", "Engraving services"], "industries": ["U.S. Army Corps of Engineers", "National Park system", "State governments", "City governments", "Industrial manufacturers"], "materials": ["Commingled post-consumer recycled plastic", "Commingled post-industrial recycled plastic", "Additives (color, UV stabilizers)"], "equipment": ["Automated production lines", "Patented custom molding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Minimum 96% recycled plastic content by weight", "Additives limited to 4% of product weight", "Patented molds and automated production lines", "Custom molding with low-cost mold design", "UV stabilizers molded in for durability"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Iowa Falls, Iowa -> /about-us", "Founded 1986 as Hammer''s Plastic Recycling -> /about-us", "Hammer''s formed Plastic Recycling, Inc. in 1984 -> /about-us", "Won Iowa Governor''s Award 1988 -> /about-us", "New management 1997, renamed 1999 -> /about-us", "Products: benches, picnic tables, planters, traffic safety, dimensional lumber, custom-molded -> / and /about-us", "Automated production lines for large-profile products -> /about-us", "Patented equipment for custom molding -> /about-us", "Unique molds protected by patents -> /about-us", "Minimum 96% recycled content, additives \u22644% -> /", "UV stabilizers molded in -> /", "Customers: U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, National Park system, state/city governments, major companies -> /", "Washington State Parks 2,000+ tables -> /", "Marshall Engines skids -> /", "Smithsonian Institution bell support -> /", "City of Norwalk hex tables -> /", "Elks Riverside Park testimonial -> /", "Mission: make plastics a community resource -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our automated production lines are used to manufacture car stops, speed bumps, landscape timbers, posts, park benches, picnic tables and other large profile products.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastic-recycling-of-iowa-falls-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plasticare, Inc. was founded in 1989 in Englewood, Colorado, and has served the Rocky Mountain region and clients across the United States for over three decades. The company operates as a fabricator and supplier of plastic and composite materials.

The shop provides custom plastic fabrication services including CNC routing, laser cutting, engraving, UV printing, saw cutting, and box fabrication. It also stocks a range of materials such as acrylic, polycarbonate, fiberglass, carbon fiber, composite resins, epoxy resins, gels, coatings, and corrugated plastic in sheet, rod, tube, and film forms. Technical consultation is offered to help customers select materials and processes.

The company ships finished components and raw materials nationwide from its Colorado facility.

The company states its mission is to empower engineers, designers, creators, and fabricators by delivering materials, precise fabrication, and technical insight, emphasizing that plastics and composites are solutions rather than substitutes. It highlights a blend of technical expertise and hands-on craftsmanship as its differentiating approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic fabrication", "Acrylic fabrication", "CNC routing", "Laser cutting", "Engraving", "UV printing", "Box fabrication", "Saw cutting", "Cut-to-size services", "Template creation", "Technical consultation", "National shipping"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Acrylic", "Polycarbonate", "Fiberglass", "Carbon fiber", "Composite resins", "Epoxy resins", "Gels", "Coatings", "Corrugated plastic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Saw cuts same day; laser/CNC cuts and UV printing 3-5 days; templates 4-5 days; box fabrication 12-14 days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day saw cuts", "3-5 day turnaround for laser/CNC cuts and UV printing", "National shipping throughout the U.S.", "Technical guidance and product recommendations", "In-stock inventory of plastic and composite materials"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Englewood, Colorado -> db", "Services: CNC routing, laser cutting, engraving, UV printing, saw cuts, box fabrication -> /", "Materials: acrylic, polycarbonate, fiberglass, carbon fiber, composite resins, epoxy resins, gels, coatings, corrugated plastic -> /", "Turnaround times: same day saw cuts, 3-5 days laser/CNC/UV, 4-5 days templates, 12-14 days box fabrication -> /", "National shipping throughout U.S. -> /", "Mission: empower engineers, designers, creators, fabricators with top-tier materials, precise fabrication, technical insight -> /", "Blend of technical expertise and hands-on craftsmanship -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From in stock inventory to custom fabrication, our team is passionate about turning challenging ideas into high end products.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plasticare' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastilite Corporation was founded in 1958 in Omaha, Nebraska. The company began as a manufacturer of expanded polystyrene products and has since expanded into cold-chain packaging solutions.

Today Plastilite produces EPS molded foam products including custom-molded trays, coolers, and insulated packaging under its IntegriTemp brand. The company recycles 100 percent of its scrap EPS foam during manufacturing and offers REfoam+, a recyclable and biodegradable foam made with 30 percent post-consumer recycled content. It also holds an exclusive NFL license for branded EPS coolers sold through grocery, convenience, and general retailers. Operations are based in the Midwest, allowing quick and cost-effective service.

The company serves healthcare, food distribution, and retail sectors, along with industrial manufacturers needing protective packaging for heavy parts, electronics, glass bottles, and ceramics. Its IntegriTemp line provides design, advice, and testing for temperature-sensitive shipments.

