foam trays for radios since 1960s -> /about-us", "EPS molded foam for integrated transport and storage systems -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Plastilite Corporation is a leading manufacturer of expanded polystyrene (EPS) products and cold-chain packaging solutions", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastilite-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastimold Products operates from a 33,000-square-foot facility in Delray Beach, Florida. The company was founded in 1999 when Joe Parisi Sr., an optical-industry veteran, purchased a small injection molding shop in Fort Lauderdale. After moves to Boca Raton (2003) and Delray Beach (2007), the business remains family-owned and is now led by second-generation owners Joe and Anthony Parisi.

The shop provides custom plastic injection molding and precision CNC machining under one roof. Its 32 all-electric presses range from 45 to 390 tons with shot sizes up to 52 ounces, supporting scientific molding, overmolding, insert molding, and in-house toolmaking. CNC capabilities include 5-axis and mill/turn machining on Makino, Okuma, Mazak, and Haas machines for aerospace alloys, medical components, and mold tooling. The company handles prototype through full-scale production, with a focus on mid-to-high volumes and short runs of 1,000–10,000 parts. Assembly services such as adhesive bonding, ultrasonic welding, and fulfillment round out the offering.

Plastimold serves OEMs in aerospace, medical, defense, firearms, consumer goods, and industrial markets. Programs often involve tight-tolerance components in high-temperature polymers (PEEK, Ultem, Delrin) and structural resins, with full traceability required by AS9100, ISO 13485, and ITAR regulations.

The company emphasizes single-source responsibility—molding, machining, tooling, and inspection stay in the same plant to shorten communication loops and maintain consistent run-to-run quality. Family ownership keeps engineering leadership close to the floor, and a gated DFM-to-delivery process aims to deliver audit-ready traceability on every shipment.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR Registered','CMMC Level 2 Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Overmolding", "Insert Molding", "Mold Manufacturing", "Precision CNC Machining (5-axis, mill/turn)", "Tooling & DFM", "Assembly (adhesive bonding, mechanical assembly, hot staking, ultrasonic welding)", "Fulfillment & Packaging", "Scientific Molding", "First Article Inspection (FAI)", "In-process Inspection", "CMM Dimensional Verification", "Material Lot Traceability", "Automated Production Cells", "Resin Selection Assistance"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Medical", "Defense", "Firearms", "Consumer Goods", "Industrial", "Automotive"], "materials": ["PEEK", "Ultem", "Delrin", "ABS", "Acetal", "Acrylic", "Nylon/GF Nylon", "PC/PC-ABS", "PP", "PE", "PET", "PS", "PVC", "TPU/TPE", "Custom Compounds"], "equipment": ["32 all-electric injection molding presses (45\u2013390 tons)", "Makino CNC machines", "Okuma CNC machines", "Mazak CNC machines", "Haas CNC machines", "In-house tool room CNC"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production; mid-to-high volume; short runs 1,000\u201310,000 parts", "lead_time": "2 business days for DFM response", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source molding and machining under one roof", "Scientific decoupled molding for consistent run-to-run quality", "Audit-ready traceability with CMM verification and material lot tracking", "In-house tooling and DFM reviews before steel is cut", "Family-owned, second-generation leadership with USA production"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 by Joe Parisi Sr. -> /about-us", "33,000 sq ft facility in Delray Beach -> /", "32 all-electric presses 45-390 tons -> /", "AS9100, ISO 13485, ISO 9001, ITAR, CMMC Level 2 -> /", "CAGE code 5ETU6 -> /", "Industries: aerospace, medical, defense, firearms, consumer goods, industrial -> /", "Materials: PEEK, Ultem, Delrin, ABS, Acetal, etc. -> /services", "Second-generation family ownership -> /about-us", "Single-source molding + machining -> /", "2-business-day DFM response -> /", "Short run 1,000-10,000 parts -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "OEMs looking for USA plastic injection molding companies and a certified plastic molder choose Plastimold for tight-tolerance plastic and machined metal parts", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "5ETU6", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Registered", "CMMC Level 2 Compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/plastimold-products/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='plastimold-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PlumtroniX, LLC, a faith-based, family-owned electronic manufacturing services provider, was established in 2010 in Springdale, Arkansas. The company expanded its capabilities in 2016 by acquiring the assets of Complete Inc., a move that broadened its assembly and integration offerings.

The company specializes in low- to medium-volume, high-mix printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) and electro-mechanical assembly. Its process portfolio includes surface-mount technology (SMT) with placement capability from 01005 components up to 55 mm packages, through-hole assembly using wave, selective, and hand soldering, and full electro-mechanical integration including wire harness and cable assembly. PlumtroniX also provides conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, urethane) and potting (epoxy, silicone) services, along with design support such as PCB layout in Altium Designer, design for manufacturability, component engineering, test development, device programming, and documentation. Product development services for microcontroller-based designs round out the offering.

