We are involved in every step of the process from start to finish to make your experience as smooth as possible.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='powerfully-green-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Powerwise Systems is based in Bucksport, Maine, and was founded in 2010. The company emerged from a team that previously worked at RainWise, Inc., a 47-year-old weather station manufacturer. Several team members helped create the PVmet line of weather stations for commercial and industrial solar PV, with more than 9,500 units installed worldwide. The chief executive is also the co-inventor of the patented SiteSage monitoring technology.

The company designs and supplies solar meteorological (MET) stations, sensors, and revenue-grade electricity, gas, and water meters for residential and commercial buildings. Its platform provides whole-house energy monitoring, BTU metering for thermal systems, and solar production tracking. Powerwise also performs MET station installation and commissioning, civil work, and ongoing operations and maintenance for large-scale photovoltaic installations.

The systems serve utility-scale solar farms, commercial rooftop arrays, and multi-tenant properties seeking granular energy cost allocation. The company’s vendor relationships span EKO Instruments, Campbell Scientific, Hukseflux, Kipp & Zonen, RainWise, RM Young, and Atonometrics.

Powerwise differentiates itself through deep domain expertise: its lead engineer authored the first edition of the SunSpec standard for weather stations, and the team brings over 40 years of weather station experience. The firm tailors MET systems to project specifications and budgets, offering a single source for hardware, installation, and long-term service.', certifications=ARRAY['LEED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar MET station design and supply", "Weather station installation and commissioning", "Civil work services for MET stations", "Operations and maintenance (O&M) for MET stations", "Revenue-grade electricity metering", "Gas and water metering", "Whole-house energy monitoring", "BTU metering for thermal energy", "Solar PV performance monitoring", "Solar resource assessment", "Solar PV weather station deployment", "Energy use tracking by tenant, circuit, or building"], "industries": ["Solar PV (commercial and industrial)", "Utility-scale solar", "Residential energy management", "Commercial building energy management", "Gas and water metering", "Thermal energy measurement"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["PVmet weather stations", "SiteSage monitoring technology", "Revenue-grade electricity meters", "BTU meters", "Whole-house monitoring systems", "Solar PV weather stations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["More than 9,500 MET stations installed worldwide", "Lead engineer authored the first SunSpec standard for weather stations", "Access to all key PV industry vendors (EKO Instruments, Campbell Scientific, Hukseflux, Kipp & Zonen, RainWise, RM Young, Atonometrics)", "Turnkey MET station installation, commissioning, civil work, and O&M services", "CEO co-inventor of patented SiteSage monitoring technology"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 -> db", "Headquarters Bucksport, Maine -> db", "Team from RainWise, 47-year weather station company -> /", "PVmet line, 9,500+ installations worldwide -> /", "Lead engineer authored SunSpec standard -> /", "CEO co-inventor of SiteSage technology -> /", "Offers solar MET stations, sensors, electricity/gas/water meters -> /", "Provides installation, commissioning, civil work, O&M -> /", "Serves solar developers, building owners, property managers -> /", "Vendor relationships with EKO Instruments, Campbell Scientific, etc. -> /", "LEED certification -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PowerWise is a proven innovator of monitoring and control technology.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='powerwise-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pratt (Bell Packaging), Inc., operating as Pratt Industries, is headquartered in Wyoming, Michigan. Founded in 1985, the company is privately held and has grown into the fifth-largest corrugated packaging company in the United States and the world''s largest privately held producer of 100% recycled containerboard.

The company operates a vertically integrated supply chain that spans 19 recycling facilities, six paper mills, 21 corrugating plants, 25 converting plants, 17 retail display facilities, and 46 transportation facilities. Its hub-and-spoke network collects recyclable materials while delivering finished boxes, feeding recovered fiber into its mills to produce 100% recycled paper for corrugated sheets, packaging, and displays. A customer team of over 300 supports design, logistics, and supply-chain management.

Pratt serves a range of industries with a noted focus on the Southeast agriculture market, providing custom corrugated boxes, palletized truckloads, and retail displays. Its logistics division manages dedicated fleets, brokerage, and shipping agency services for local, regional, and national distribution.

The company''s differentiation rests on its "green mission" — using recycling as a tool against climate change — and its independence as a privately held business that prioritizes people, customers, and the planet. In 2022, executive chairman Anthony Pratt pledged a $5 billion investment in U.S. recycling and clean energy infrastructure, aiming to create 5,000 manufacturing jobs by 2032.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Recycling collection and material recovery", "100% recycled paper mill production", "Corrugating and converting", "Retail display manufacturing", "Custom corrugated packaging design", "Full-service logistics (dedicated fleet, brokerage, shipping agency)", "Supply-chain management", "Hub-and-spoke distribution", "Close-the-loop recycling program"], "industries": ["Agriculture"], "materials": ["100% recycled paper", "Old corrugated containers (OCC)", "Containerboard", "Corrugated sheets"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated supply chain from recycling to finished packaging", "100% recycled containerboard produced in-house", "Nationwide hub-and-spoke logistics network with dedicated fleet", "Privately held independence guiding long-term decisions", "$5 billion pledge for U.S. recycling and clean energy investment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Wyoming, Michigan -> db", "Founded 1985 -> db and homepage ''Serving North America Since 1985''", "Privately held -> homepage ''Pratt Industries is privately held''", "Fifth largest corrugated packaging company in US -> homepage", "World''s largest privately held producer of 100% recycled containerboard -> homepage", "19 recycling facilities, 6 paper mills, 21 corrugating plants, 25 converting plants, 17 retail display facilities, 46 transportation facilities -> homepage", "Hub-and-spoke network collecting recyclables during delivery -> homepage", "Customer team over 300 strong -> homepage", "Serves Southeast agricu