UPDATE companies SET description='Prince Manufacturing Corporation traces its roots to 1941, when John Prince opened a small machine shop on Water Street in Sioux City, Iowa, under the name Prince Hydraulics. His son Richard incorporated the business in September 1950 after securing a contract for 100 single-acting hydraulic cylinders, with Arthur C. Gall and F. John Roost joining as vice president and secretary/treasurer. The company now operates from North Sioux City, South Dakota.

