UPDATE companies SET description='Propper Manufacturing Company, Inc. operates from Long Island City, New York. Founded in 1945, the family-owned business has remained under family stewardship for nearly eight decades. The company was established to address sterilization monitoring needs in healthcare settings.

The company manufactures disposable medical devices with a focus on sterilization monitoring. Its product line includes chemical indicators (Type 1 and Type 5), biological indicators (Duo-Spore®), Bowie-Dick test packs, EO sterilization monitoring tools (including the FDA-cleared EO Chex™ indicator tape), and reusable process challenge devices (Vapor Line® Helix-Type PCD). They also produce Magnalume™ disposable laryngoscope blades made from high-strength polycarbonate, microscope slides, cover glass, hemacytometers, surgical blades, and other laboratory and surgical instruments. The facility offers private labeling and OEM manufacturing services, and runs a Culture Service Program for biological monitoring.

Propper serves hospitals, laboratories, veterinary clinics, dental offices, biotech and pharmaceutical companies, scientific research institutions, and body modification professionals. The company also supports international markets and provides OEM solutions for major healthcare brands.

The company states its mission is to provide high-quality infection control products that aid in eliminating hospital-acquired infections. It emphasizes investment in groundbreaking products and customer education through platforms like Propper Connects.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA clearance (EO Chex™ Ethylene Oxide Indicator Tape)','ISO 7376 Green System compatibility','ISO & FDA compliant (OEM solutions)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sterilization monitoring device manufacturing", "Chemical indicator production (Type 1, Type 5)", "Biological indicator production (Duo-Spore\u00ae)", "Bowie-Dick test pack manufacturing", "Ethylene oxide (EO) sterilization monitoring", "Reusable process challenge device (PCD) manufacturing", "Disposable laryngoscope blade manufacturing (polycarbonate)", "Microscope slide and cover glass manufacturing", "Surgical blade and instrument manufacturing", "Private labeling services", "OEM contract manufacturing", "Culture Service Program (biological monitoring service)", "Cleaning efficacy testing", "Protein detection testing", "Washer-disinfector monitoring", "Ultrasonic bath monitoring", "Packaging and record keeping products", "Waste containment products"], "industries": ["Healthcare / Hospitals", "Dental and Endodontic", "Veterinary / Animal Health", "Biotechnology", "Pharmaceutical", "Scientific Research", "Body Modification", "International markets", "OEM / Medical device manufacturers"], "materials": ["Polycarbonate", "Glass", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only FDA-cleared ethylene oxide indicator tape on the U.S. market (EO Chex\u2122)", "Vapor Line\u00ae Integrator provides easy-to-read PASS/FAIL for steam sterilization", "Reusable Helix-Type PCD (Vapor Line\u00ae Reusable Sterilization Process Challenge Test) for cost-effective, eco-friendly high-volume monitoring", "Family-owned with decades of experience since 1945", "Manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Long Island City, New York -> db", "Founded: 1945 -> /about", "Ownership: Family-owned -> /about", "Company type: Manufacturer of disposable medical devices -> /about", "Specialization: Sterilization monitoring devices and services -> /about", "Products: Chemical indicators (Type 1, Type 5), biological indicators (Duo-Spore\u00ae), Bowie-Dick test packs, EO Chex\u2122 indicator tape, Vapor Line\u00ae Integrator, Vapor Line\u00ae Reusable PCD -> /, /about", "Magnalume\u2122 disposable laryngoscope blades (polycarbonate, ISO 7376) -> /", "Microscope slides, cover glass, hemacytometers, surgical blades -> /", "Services: Private labeling, OEM, Culture Service Program -> /, /about", "Industries: Healthcare, dental, veterinary, biotech, pharmaceutical, scientific research, body modification, international, OEM -> /, /about", "FDA clearance for EO Chex\u2122 -> /", "ISO 7376 Green System compatibility -> /", "Mission: Infection control products to eliminate hospital-acquired infections -> /about", "Manufactured in USA -> /about", "President & CEO: Joe Looney (Medical) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Propper Manufacturing Company, Inc. is a leading manufacturer of disposable medical devices specializing in sterilization monitoring devices and services.", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='propper-manufacturing-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Proto Part Inc. operates from Hudson, New Hampshire, where it has been producing thermoplastic injection molded parts for over 25 years. The company emphasizes American manufacturing and win-win relationships, though its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The shop specializes in thermoplastic injection molding with all tooling built in-house. Capabilities include insert molding, family molding, and design-for-manufacturability support, running on horizontal and vertical presses ranging from 28 to 310 clamping tons with shot sizes of 1 to 25 ounces. Processes follow scientific injection molding and decoupled molding principles, with ongoing automation investments to increase efficiency. Production volumes span from hundreds to hundreds of thousands of parts per run, covering both mid- and high-volume orders.

Proto Part serves medical, defense, safety, electronic/electrical, industrial, aerospace, solar, and automotive markets, as well as niche consumer products such as cribbage pegs, golf tees, tape containers, and archery bowstring spools. Long-term customers include Semiconductor Circuits Inc., Road Tools LLC, Mirror Tee, RF Hunter, and Wall Industries, with relationships exceeding 20 years in some cases.

