UPDATE companies SET description='QT Corporation is based in Wilson, North Carolina, and has been building custom electrical panels since 1994. The company is led by President Jimmy Sauls, Application Engineer Tyson Sauls, and Sales Representative Mark Sauls.

The shop specializes in the design, fabrication, wiring, and installation of OEM panels, industrial automation control panels, and switchgear protection and control panels. All assemblies are built to UL 508A and NEC standards, and every unit undergoes 100 percent functional testing before shipment. The facility, expanded in 2005, supports both low- and high-volume runs and offers just-in-time delivery to customers within a 2.5-hour radius of Wilson.

QT Corporation serves original-equipment manufacturers, industrial automation integrators, and electrical switchgear builders across the United States and internationally. Project examples include substation protection and control panels, interposing relay panels, and custom industrial control panels that integrate directly into machinery or plant processes.

The company emphasizes its decades of combined engineering and wiring experience, a strategic ordering process that lowers material costs, and on-site warranty service to support panels after installation. Fixtures and jigs are designed for each job to reduce assembly time, and the team works to help clients “move power forward” with cost-effective, reliable panel solutions.', certifications=ARRAY['UL 508A','NEC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom panel design", "Panel fabrication", "Industrial wiring", "Panel installation", "Engineering services", "UL 508A compliant panel building", "100% functional testing", "Just-in-time delivery", "On-site warranty service", "Fixture and jig design for assembly", "Switchboard/switchgear control panel fabrication", "Industrial control panel fabrication", "OEM panel fabrication", "Substation protection and control panel fabrication"], "industries": ["OEM manufacturing", "Industrial automation", "Electrical switchgear", "Substation protection and control"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL 508A authorized for over 20 years", "100% functional testing on every panel before delivery", "Just-in-time delivery within a 2.5\u2011hour radius of Wilson, NC", "On\u2011site warranty service after installation", "Decades of combined experience in panel engineering, wiring, and fabrication"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 -> db", "Headquarters Wilson, NC -> db", "UL 508A authorized for over 20 years -> /about", "100% functionality testing before delivery -> /about", "Just-in-time delivery within 2.5-hour radius -> /about", "On-site warranty service -> /about", "Facility expanded 2005 -> /about", "Management team: Jimmy Sauls (President), Tyson Sauls (Application Engineer), Mark Sauls (Sales Rep) -> /about", "Serves OEM, industrial automation, switchgear, substation protection -> /", "Custom panel design, fabrication, wiring, installation -> /about", "Built to UL & NEC guidelines -> /", "Decades of combined experience -> /about", "Strategic ordering and dealer network for cost savings -> /", "Fixtures and jigs designed per job -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom panel design, fabrication and installation", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='q-t-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='QBit Semiconductor LTD. was founded in 2016 in Littleton, Massachusetts, by a core R&D team that originated from Qualcomm''s imaging-processing engineering group.

The company develops highly integrated SOCs that combine precision motion control, intelligent image processing, and energy-aware sensing management. A next-generation QB7xxx series featuring an ARM Cortex-A76 processor is under development. QBit maintains R&D subsidiaries in Boston (QBIT USA) and Tokyo (QBIT JP).

QBit''s chips serve markets including multifunction printers, printers, medical devices, intelligent self-service systems, photo printers, point-of-sale terminals, kiosks, robotics, and drones. Strategic investors and partners include ARM, TSMC, Qualcomm, and Sony, the latter having awarded QBit its Green Partner certification.

